.TH LOCALPIN 1 "2026-10-18" "LocalPIN" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
localpin, localpinctl \- manage local desktop PIN credentials
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B localpin
.RI [ global-options ] " command " [ arguments ]
.br
.B localpin
.RI [ global-options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
LocalPIN adds opt-in PIN or passcode unlocking to an existing local Fedora KDE
session. The account password remains available for unlocking and recovery.
Initial login, text consoles, sudo, SSH, polkit and disk encryption retain their
existing authentication requirements.
.PP
With no command, LocalPIN prints concise help and exits without interaction or
broker contact. Use
.B menu
for the optional interactive menu or
.B setup
for guided onboarding. The compatibility name
.B localpinctl
has the same behavior.
.PP
LocalPIN is experimental authentication software without a supported production
release. Start in a disposable Fedora KDE 44 x86_64 VM with SELinux enforcing.
Independent security review and physical hardware validation remain open.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help. A command followed by this option shows focused command help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the installed version.
.TP
.BR \-\-color " " auto|always|never
Choose color policy for human output; also accepts
.BR \-\-color=VALUE .
Auto honors the output destination,
.B NO_COLOR
and
.BR TERM=dumb .
JSON and completion source are always undecorated.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-input
Refuse commands that need interaction before terminal access, account inspection
or broker contact. This does not supply confirmation or allow secret input from
a pipe. Status, diagnostics, help, version, completions and integration guidance
remain available.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B menu
Open the optional inline numbered menu in a foreground terminal.
.TP
.B setup
Set up or resume onboarding as the normal desktop owner. Explain preparation,
choose protection, enroll privately, guide real trial and recovery checks, and
request explicit activation. Supported accounting maintenance requires explicit
approval to save work and sign out. Resume decisions use protected system state.
Preparation offers the full policy diff on request before a separate apply
confirmation; pausing the review applies nothing.
.TP
.BR status " [\-\-json]"
Show own-account enrollment, backend, availability, cooldown and desktop gate.
.TP
.BR doctor " [\-\-json]"
Show readiness and actionable diagnostics. Passive checks do not perform desktop
unlock tests, password recovery tests or TPM enrollment.
.TP
.B enroll \-\-backend auto|tpm2-required|software
Create a PIN or passcode after confirmation and fresh account-password
verification. Both auto and tpm2-required attempt TPM creation and verification;
software protection must be selected explicitly.
.TP
.B change
Replace your credential on the existing backend, with fresh password verification.
.TP
.B disable
Disable your own credential after fresh password verification. This does not
restore the system's desktop authentication configuration.
.TP
.B migrate \-\-backend tpm2-required|software
Explicitly replace the protection backend and credential. The target must differ
from the current backend.
.TP
.B integration status
Inspect the desktop integration gate without contacting the broker.
.TP
.B integration enable
Show the separate administrator activation command and its preparation, trial,
desktop/password-test and recovery prerequisites. This command does not activate.
.TP
.B integration disable
Show the separate administrator command to disable system integration.
.TP
.B recover \-\-user ACCOUNT
As an already-root caller, disable the named existing non-root local account's
credential through the broker. Never reveal a PIN or repair account authority.
.TP
.B help "[COMMAND [SUBCOMMAND]]"
Show full help or focused command help. Also accepts COMMAND followed by
.BR \-\-help " or " \-h .
.TP
.B completions bash|zsh|fish
Print static completion source. The RPM installs completions for both command
names. Scripts suggest public commands, flags and closed choices without
querying accounts, the broker or credential state.
.SH CREDENTIAL INPUT
Numeric PINs permit 4-16 digits with TPM protection and 8-16 digits with software
protection. Both permit an explicitly selected printable-ASCII passcode of 8-64
characters, preserving spaces and case. Recommendations are 6 TPM digits,
10 software digits and 12 or more passcode characters. Legacy six-digit software
credentials remain usable with replacement advice.
.PP
Secrets require terminal stdin and a real foreground controlling terminal.
New credentials show asterisks; account passwords remain hidden. Never supply
secrets through command arguments, environment variables, stdin or pipes.
Cancellation restores terminal settings. A failed or uncertain commit requires
checking status before retrying.
.SH OUTPUT
Status and doctor accept
.B \-\-json
for nonsecret schema-version-2 output. This includes own-user credential type,
length and policy metadata, never the credential value. Installed, enrolled,
trial, tested and active states are distinct. Installation and enrollment alone
do not activate PIN unlocking. Operator attestations are not independent proof
that a real unlock or recovery test was performed.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including help and a quietly closed output pipe.
.TP
.B 1
Operational failure, including unavailable state or refused interaction.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command or arguments. Rejected argument values are not repeated.
.TP
.B 130
Cancelled operation.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable automatic color output. An explicit color option selects its own policy.
.TP
.B TERM
A value of dumb disables automatic color output.
.PP
LocalPIN-specific secret and simulator environment channels are rejected;
there is no environment mechanism for passing credentials.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
localpin
localpin help setup
localpin setup
localpin --no-input status --json
localpin --color=never doctor
localpin completions bash
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sudo (8),
.BR pam (8),
.BR authselect (8)
.PP
The packaged integration and account administration runbooks describe guarded
activation, actual password/console recovery tests and removal. The project
usage guide is available at https://github.com/tommcamm/LocalPIN/blob/main/docs/usage.md.
